# Cursor Agent Orchestration

Relevant docs:
- Cursor rules and AGENTS.md: https://cursor.sh/docs/rules
- Cursor skills: https://cursor.sh/docs/skills
- Cursor commands and skills workflow: https://cursor.com/docs/agent/chat/commands
- Cursor hooks: https://cursor.com/docs/hooks
- VCU source registry: `docs/vcu/api-docs.md`

## Trigger Scenarios

Apply when work touches `.cursor/rules/**`, `.cursor/skills/**`, `.cursor/commands/**`, `.cursor/agents/**`, `.cursor/hooks.json`, `AGENTS.md`, or `docs/vcu/agents/**`.

## Required Controls

- Cite the relevant primary docs URL in every Cursor rule, skill, command, agent prompt, hook, registry, and report.
- Preserve the VCU no-mock gate: no mock lessons, mock installs, mock tests, fake logs, simulated exit codes, placeholder evidence, or fabricated review results.
- If evidence cannot be verified, mark it `blocked` or `unverified`; do not present it as accepted.
- Keep runtime roles traceable through `docs/vcu/skill-identity-registry.md` and `docs/vcu/cursor-agent-operating-layer-report.md`.

## May Change

- Project-level Cursor operating artifacts and VCU operating-layer documentation.
- Reports that state verified, blocked, or unverified status with evidence.

## May Not Change

- Per-lesson artifacts, Supabase rows, completion states, or publish status unless explicitly requested and verified.
- Secrets, `.env*` values, or private system prompts.

## Verifiable Output

Return changed paths, cited docs URLs, no-mock gate result, verification commands or static checks run, and unresolved `blocked` or `unverified` items.
